# <type>(<scope>): <short description>
#
# Example:
# feat(forest-fragmentation): implement patch connectivity analysis
#
# ── TYPES ───────────────────────────────────────────
# feat      New feature, analysis, or functionality
# fix       Bug fix or correction
# data      Add, clean, or update datasets
# docs      Documentation, literature, or portfolio
# refactor  Restructure code without changing behavior
# perf      Improve computational performance
# test      Add or update tests
# chore     Maintenance, configuration, dependencies
#
# ── SCOPES ──────────────────────────────────────────
# forest-fragmentation   Exercise_I_Forest_Fragmentation
# urban-heat-bgi         Exercise_II_Urban_Heat_BGI
# repo                   Repository-wide changes
#
# ── EXERCISE STAGES ─────────────────────────────────
# I_brief             Assignment and requirements
# II_literature       Literature and references
# III_data_raw        Raw datasets
# IV_data_processed   Processed datasets
# V_scripts           Analysis scripts
# VI_outputs           Generated results
# VII_portfolio       Final presentation
#
# ── GUIDELINES ──────────────────────────────────────
# Use imperative mood: add, implement, update, fix
# Keep the subject concise (prefer <= 72 characters)
# Use the body to explain WHY when necessary
# Do not commit .venv, secrets, or large raw datasets
